## Interaction run (CDP, real mouse input)

A temporary out-of-repo helper drove Chrome for Testing (Playwright chromium-1248, headless) through
CDP: `Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride` (1440×900 and 390×844, DPR 1),
`Emulation.setEmulatedMedia` (reduced motion), `Input.dispatchMouseEvent` (real pointer events
with capture), `Runtime.evaluate` (state read-out only) and `Page.captureScreenshot`. It was kept
outside the repository. State lines: frame mode / orientation / x,y,w,h (world px), landing slot,
item state@x,y and detach progress, edge count and the status line.

