Reading of the run:

- **1:1 tracking** — pointer +120 px moves the item centre by exactly +120 px.
- **Pull out** — mid-drag the frame already shrinks to the notepad (274×123) and the notepad keeps
  its place; release commits the detach.
- **Dock back** — over the zone the frame grows back, the landing slot shows, the drop on top of the
  notepad keeps the stacked orientation (overlap rule).
- **Reorder** — dragging the photo up past the notepad moves the notepad down (makes room) while the
  frame stays; release: "Order changed inside the zone."
- **Side by side** — dragging the photo beside the notepad switches to horizontal; the notepad stays
  where it was and the frame re-forms around it; release: "Orientation changed inside the zone."
- **Emptying / collapse** — pulling the last item out dims the frame (dashed); release fades it out
  (collapsed) and announces the hidden zone.
- **Group** — the notepad over the photo shows a dashed ghost frame around the photo (which does not
  move; clamped at the right edge); moving away removes it, coming back shows it again; release forms
  the zone: "Items grouped stacked into a new zone."
- **Resize** — 1440 → 390: the zone keeps its relative place, stays inside, no horizontal overflow.
- **Reduced motion** — all zone transitions compute to 0s; a detach lands at once.
- **Motion** — items: `translate 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1)`, lift `scale 0.15s`; frame:
  `transform 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1)` (FLIP resize), opacity, no width/height transition,
  no overshoot.
- **Edge** — exactly one edge element in every state.

